{
  "_": "The standup's dates read (docs/modules/solitaire-agile.md, \"What moved, and the window\"): ONE gh api graphql call per repo (per 50 aliases), the owner and name as variables. `query` is the text both halves send for its hashes and numbers, line for line (dates_query / Get-P20StandupDatesQuery): c<i> is the i-th hash's commit by object(expression:), i<n> issue n's labelled and assigned events. Each case is the parse of one answer's `repository` object (dates_from_answer / ConvertFrom-P20StandupDates): a commit is dated by its authoredDate only when GitHub resolved the hash to a commit whose oid begins with it -- an abbreviated hash resolves, a missing or ambiguous one answers null and is null here, never a guess; an issue's start is the earliest of a worker label being added and the issue being assigned, a label that routes to no worker is not a start, and an issue with no start is not a key of issueStarts. Asserted from tkTestToolkit -Rituals and Tests/test_rituals.py.",
